## Abstract Repository — budget_repository.dart
```dart
abstract class BudgetRepository {
  Future<List<Budget>> getBudgetsByMonth(int year, int month);
  Future<Budget?> getBudgetByCategory(String categoryId, int year, int month);
  Future<void> addBudget(Budget budget);
  Future<void> updateBudget(Budget budget);
  Future<void> deleteBudget(String id);
  Future<List<BudgetProgress>> getBudgetProgress(int year, int month);
  // Calculates spent amount by joining with transactions
}
```

## Get Budget Progress Use Case
```dart
class GetBudgetProgress {
  final BudgetRepository budgetRepo;
  final TransactionRepository transactionRepo;

  GetBudgetProgress(this.budgetRepo, this.transactionRepo);

  Future<List<BudgetProgress>> call(int year, int month) async {
    final budgets = await budgetRepo.getBudgetsByMonth(year, month);
    final transactions = await transactionRepo.getTransactionsByMonth(year, month);

    return budgets.map((budget) {
      final spent = transactions
          .where((tx) =>
              tx.type == TransactionType.expense &&
              tx.categoryId == budget.categoryId)
          .fold(0, (sum, tx) => sum + tx.amount);

      return BudgetProgress(budget: budget, spentAmount: spent);
    }).toList();
  }
}
```

## Screen Specifications

### budget_page.dart
- Accessed from Home screen or Settings
- AppBar: large title "Budget"
- MonthSelector at top (same widget as History/Report)
- List of BudgetProgressCard widgets per category
- Total budget summary at top: total limit vs total spent
- FAB: "+" → add_budget_page.dart
- Empty state: "No budgets set for this month" + "Set Budget" button
- Swipe to delete budget

### add_budget_page.dart
- Modal bottom sheet
- Category picker: same grid (only expense categories shown)
- Budget limit: numeric input (formatRupiah)
- Month: pre-selected as current month (can change)
- Save button: full-width black ElevatedButton
- Validation: cannot add duplicate category for same month

### budget_progress_card.dart Widget
```dart
BudgetProgressCard({
  required BudgetProgress progress,
  required VoidCallback onDelete,
})
```
Layout:
- Row: category icon + label (left) | spent / limit amounts (right)
- LinearProgressIndicator below:
  - Normal (< 80%):  black fill, gray track
  - Warning (>= 80%): dark gray fill, gray track
  - Exceeded (100%+): black fill with striped pattern
- Percentage text: right-aligned below bar
- If exceeded: show "Over budget" label in dark gray

### budget_alert_banner.dart Widget
```dart
// Shown on Home page when any budget >= 80%
BudgetAlertBanner({
  required List<BudgetProgress> warnings,
  required VoidCallback onTap,
})
```
- Black background, white text
- Text: "⚠ 2 budgets are near limit" (or "exceeded")
- Tap → navigate to budget_page.dart
- Dismissible (user can close)
- Only shown when there are warnings

